    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0201" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1413.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Italy to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Foreign Minister says that while conditions in the Chinese Republic remain
                    precarious and provisional, formal recognition would be premature. It is the
                    duty of the Powers to make sure that the Government can effectively assume
                    obligations. The Italian Government will therefore wait and observe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Brien</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
